    "created_at": "2015-11-17T01:04:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-17T01:04:30Z",
    "body": "The isolation rules are there so that if you change the 'display' of the ruby (e.g. to show it inline, parenthesized, which is better when the text is already very small) the bidi ordering doesn't get mixed up.\n",
